messages:
eva_support: Customer reports intermittent OAuth callback failures for both Google and GitHub. Symptoms: `invalid_grant: PKCE verifier mismatch` or `state mismatch` after redirect. Happens ~5% of attempts, mostly mobile users behind corporate proxies. Ticket #12345. Repro steps and logs below.

aj_platform: Can you paste an example redirect URL (redacted) and note which redirect_uri/client app? Also any browser or proxy details?

eva_support: Example (customer-captured):
```
https://app.redwood.ai/auth/callback?code=SplxlOBeZQQYbYS6WxSbIA&state=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMjM0NTY3ODkwIiwiaWF0IjoxNjE2MjM5MDIyfQ.SflKxwRJSMeKKF2QT4fwpMeJf36POk6yJV_adQssw5c++%20%25&scope=openid%20email
```
Note: `state` contains `+`, encoded spaces and percent signs and is ~700+ chars for this customer (they encode an eval payload + metadata). They route via Fastly -> corporate proxy -> mobile carrier.

eva_support: Callback logs (redacted):
```
callback.ts:224 Received querystring length=1789
callback.ts:226 req.query.state="eyJhbGci..." (truncated) length=256
session store: state="eyJhbGci...long..." length=713
Result: state mismatch -> reject
```
So our stored state is full length, but the incoming `state` is truncated/changed.

eng-bot: alert: oauth.callback.state-mismatch fired 11 times in last 48h for tenant=enterprise-xyz. Aggregated top user-agent: Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone). Link: https://ops.redwood.ai/incidents/INC-2025-332

manny_prod: My hunch: (1) some proxies/caches normalize `+` to space when URL-decoding, (2) querystring truncation by intermediate device for very long URLs, (3) cookie/session splits if state stored in cookie/header and exceeds size. Short-term mitigation: stop putting full payload in `state` -> store full state server-side and send a short token/hash in the URL.

zara_auth: Can you confirm request headers from a failing trace? Need `Via`, `X-Forwarded-*`, and any reproxy headers. Also which CDN (Fastly/Cloudflare) and if they have max-url settings.

eva_support: Provided by customer (redacted):
```
Via: 1.1 proxy.corp
X-Forwarded-For: 10.2.3.4
X-Forwarded-Proto: https
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 15_5 like Mac OS X)
Referer: https://app.example-corp.com/
```
They confirm occasional redirect length > 3000 chars. They also saw their corporate proxy replace `+` with space on incoming request line.

zara_auth: OK that explains it. Two actionable items: A) short-term mitigation (rollout today) -> switch to server-side state store with a short token in URL, and B) improve logging and safe fallback so we don't throw hard on mismatch (e.g., show a friendly page and a way to retry). Proposed quick middleware (pseudo):
```
// short token + server-side state cache
app.get('/auth/start', (req, res) => {
  const fullState = JSON.stringify({v:1, payload: heavyObject});
  const id = randomId(8); // 8 chars
  cache.set('oauth_state:' + id, fullState, 300);
  const redirect = buildOAuthUrl({state: id});
  res.redirect(redirect);
});

app.get('/auth/callback', (req, res) => {
  const token = req.query.state;
  const stored = cache.get('oauth_state:' + token);
  if (!stored) {
    log.warn("state missing", {token, len: (req.query.state||'').length});
    return res.status(400).send('State mismatch. Please retry (we logged details).');
  }
  // proceed with PKCE verification using stored payload
});
```
Also, if we keep any state in a cookie, ensure `SameSite=None; Secure` and avoid splitting large cookies.

aj_platform: Good. Can we add a logging enhancement: on state-mismatch, log raw `request.url.length`, `req.headers.via`, and UA. Also add high-cardinality tag for `tenant` so we can track which customers are hitting this.

zara_auth: I'll open a feature-flagged PR that implements the short-token flow and the extra logs. PR will include a unit test that simulates `+ -> space` and truncated querystring. Plan: open PR today, tests + review tonight, canary rollout to staging tomorrow morning. If we see reduced errors, roll to prod.

eva_support: I've communicated the temporary workaround to the customer: ask users to try a non-proxied network or desktop browser, or ask their proxy team to allow long querystrings/unescape `+` behavior. Customer accepted the mitigation for now.

manny_prod: Long-term: update our docs + SDKs to never put bulky payloads in `state`. Use a reference token or signed short JWT <= 64 chars. Also consider POST-based handoff (Auth server posts back via form POST) where supported.

ez: thanks all — marking ticket as assigned to `zara_auth` and leaving open until canary is green. :thumbsup:
